      "title": "[acceptance] flashblocks: load tests",
      "author": "yashvardhan-kukreja",
      "number": 379,
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/infra",
      "body": "A basic load test simulating a 20-30 RPS traffic against the flashblocks-enabled network.\n\nThe test's expectation to still continuing noticing a healthy stream of flashblocks still producing at a 250ms rate.\n\n",
      "createdAt": "2025-05-28T06:10:24Z",
      "closedAt": "2026-01-09T22:01:00Z",
      "state": "CLOSED",
      "commentCount": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "I_kwDOL-xLQ862jNrS",
      "title": "[acceptance] test: flashblocks: sequencer failover when all rollup-boost instances are unhealthy",
      "author": "alfonso-op",
      "number": 350,
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/infra",
      "body": "We need to test the specific failure mode where the rollup-boost instance for all rollup-boost-enabled sequencers is down or unhealthy.\n\nIn such a case, conductor should successfully transfer leadership to a sequencer that is not running rollup-boost.\n\nFor more info, see https://github.com/ethereum-optimism/optimism/issues/15874",
      "createdAt": "2025-05-14T10:49:40Z",
      "closedAt": "2026-01-09T21:59:47Z",
      "state": "CLOSED",
      "commentCount": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "I_kwDOL-xLQ862Il6V",
      "title": "[acceptance] test: flashblocks HA failover",
      "author": "scharissis",
      "number": 318,
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/infra",
      "body": "Flashblocks requires TX ingress to be sent to an op-rbuilder which is peered with active sequencers, validating an HA solution for this and testing should be apart of this acceptance plan.\n\nFlashblocks failover behavior may be different depending on if you failover after the first flashblock, somewhere in the middle of the series of flashblocks within a regular block slot or at the end of it. These variations of the above more general failure modes should be covered.",
      "createdAt": "2025-05-12T05:48:12Z",
      "closedAt": "2026-01-09T21:59:41Z",
      "state": "CLOSED",
      "commentCount": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "I_kwDOL-xLQ862IlYe",
      "title": "[acceptance] test: rbuilder failure",
      "author": "scharissis",
      "number": 317,
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/infra",
      "body": "A sequencer with default EL block building is selected when rbuilder fails for all sequencers.",
      "createdAt": "2025-05-12T05:46:41Z",
      "closedAt": "2026-01-09T21:59:36Z",
